  "habitat": "Thickets and rank grass in thornveld, and riparian and secondary growth around cultivated land. Drier places than African Firefinch.",
  "summary": "A common resident, the reddest firefinch. The bill is blackish in both sexes. The male has the crown, nape and mantle washed pink, rose-pink underparts, and upper parts less dark than African Firefinch. The female is more orange-pink below. The immature male is more uniformly brown above, rose-pink below, with a brownish wash on the side of the breast. Calls include a tinkling trrr-trrr alarm, tewee-tewee, fweeee and zik-zik. The Kemp code RB was left unchanged.",
